[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_ralph"
text = "# DRAFT
# Ralph the chandler at the Cross Keys, night 0. He makes the abbey's candles; his daughter Kit sells them.
# The sacrist has bought far more candles since about Michaelmas, and pays in coin the abbey never used to have.
== start
(A thin man with wax under his nails and old burns on his fingers, nursing a small ale.)
Ralph: From the abbey, are you? Then you're my best customer, brother, whether you know it or not.
-> topics

== again
Ralph: Brother. Tell your sacrist I've wax enough for whatever he wants.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n0_ralph_candles] (Ask what he means.) -> candles
* [if n0_ralph_candles] [if not n0_ralph_coin] (Ask how the sacrist pays.) -> coin
* [if not n0_ralph_kit] (Ask after his trade.) -> trade

== candles [set n0_ralph_candles]
Ralph: Ralph, chandler. Every candle in that church came out of my shop.
Ralph: Your sacrist, Brother Ranulf, buys more than he ever did. Twice what he bought at Easter, and more again.
Ralph: Since about Michaelmas. I asked him once what they burn them all for. He didn't say.
-> topics

== coin [set n0_ralph_coin]
Ralph: In coin. Good silver, on the nail, and he doesn't haggle.
Ralph: That abbey hadn't two pennies to rub together. Everybody knew it. Now it's silver.
Ralph: I don't ask where a man of God gets his silver. I'm a chandler. I sell candles.
-> topics

== trade [set n0_ralph_kit]
Ralph: Wax for the altar, tallow for the rest. It's a living, if you don't mind the stink.
Ralph: My girl Kit sells them in the lane. She's at your gate most dusks with her tray. Be kind to her.
-> topics

== leave
Ralph: Good night, brother. Pray for the price of wax.
"
